    {
      "id": "evidence-000-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Certificate: order 1, recurrence coefficients a_0 = m + n - p, a_1 = -(p + 1), R(p,k) = k*(k + n - p) / (p - k + 1). The certificate identity is symbolic in ALL of m, n, p, k -- four variables -- so the recurrence is established for symbolic m and n, not merely at sample values. The closed form is not claimed by this fact; turning the recurrence into C(m+n,p) needs the base case S(0) = 1 at symbolic m and n, which lane `telescoping-scale` later established -- see F:chu-vandermonde-convolution.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
